{"modified-p": false, "id": "gomodel:6ac817cf00001061", "individuals": [{"id": "gomodel:6ac817cf00001061/6ac817cf00001062", "type": [{"type": "class", "id": "GO:0015277", "label": "kainate selective glutamate receptor activity"}], "root-type": [{"type": "class", "id": "GO:0003674", "label": "molecular_function"}, {"type": "class", "id": "obo:go/extensions/reacto.owl#molecular_event", "label": "Molecular Event"}], "annotations": [{"key": "contributor", "value": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5283-6593"}, {"key": "providedBy", "value": "https://www.uniprot.org"}, {"key": "date", "value": "2026-10-12"}]}, {"id": "gomodel:6ac817cf00001061/6ac817cf00001063", "type": [{"type": "class", "id": "GO:0032983", "label": "kainate selective glutamate receptor complex"}], "root-type": [{"type": "class", "id": "GO:0005575", "label": "cellular_component"}, {"type": "class", "id": "GO:0032991", "label": "protein-containing complex"}], "annotations": [{"key": "contributor", "value": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5283-6593"}, {"key": "providedBy", "value": "https://www.uniprot.org"}, {"key": "comment", "value": "General: There are 5 subunits for the kainate receptor complex. The functional receptor is a tetramer (i.e. a dimer of dimers) composed of different combinations of subunits. There are expression data in macaque's retina showing expression of GRIK1 and GRIK2. GRIK1 and GRIK2 have also been shown to be able to form a functional channel. That's why I used kainate receptor complex as enabler with has part GRIK1 and GRIK2. Other combinations of GRIK1-GRIK5 surely do exist, but cannot find evidence for complex composition in the retina."}, {"key": "date", "value": "2026-10-15"}]}, {"id": "gomodel:6ac817cf00001061/6ac817cf00001064", "type": [{"type": "class", "id": "UniProtKB:P39086", "label": "GRIK1 Hsap"}], "root-type": [{"type": "class", "id": "CHEBI:33695", "label": "information biomacromolecule"}, {"type": "class", "id": "CHEBI:24431", "label": "chemical entity"}, {"type": "class",